# freebell-bk7258 settings. Copy to ~/.config/doorbell-bk7258/env (chmod 600) and uncomment
# what you need. Dotenv syntax: KEY=value, # comments, optional quotes; $HOME and ~ are expanded
# in unquoted and double-quoted values. Precedence: command-line flag > environment variable >
# this file > built-in default. Read by scripts/env.sh (bash) and tools/dbenv.py (python).
# Everything here is optional except DOORBELL_HOST (needed by tools/dbcmd.py and scripts/release.sh).

# ---- device (TCP command channel, tools/dbcmd.py, scripts/release.sh) ----
# IP or hostname of the doorbell on your LAN. No default: the tools stop with an error if unset.
#DOORBELL_HOST=192.168.1.50
# The command token you stored on the device with `tok set SECRET` (over serial). Either put it
# here (keep this file private) or point DOORBELL_TOKEN_FILE at a file with a `TOKEN=...` line.
#DOORBELL_TOKEN=
# File containing `TOKEN=...`, used when DOORBELL_TOKEN is unset. No default.
#DOORBELL_TOKEN_FILE=$HOME/.config/doorbell-bk7258/tcp_token.env

# ---- serial (BootROM flashing and the UART shell tools in tools/) ----
# UART adapter. Default: the first match of /dev/cu.usbserial-*, /dev/ttyUSB*, /dev/ttyACM*.
#SERIAL_PORT=/dev/cu.usbserial-XXXX

# ---- build (scripts/build.sh, scripts/flash.sh) ----
# Where finished images land (doorbell-fw_<ver>_app_pack.rbl / _avdk_all-app.bin and the doorbell-fw_latest_* links).
#FW_DIR=$HOME/data/doorbell-bk7258/firmware
# Build directory (default ~/data/doorbell-bk7258/avdk-build); the build writes to $OUT/doorbell/...
#OUT=$HOME/data/doorbell-bk7258/avdk-build
# Beken SDK checkouts (bekencorp/bk_idk and bk_avdk, branch release/v2.0.1).
#SDK=$HOME/reps/oss/bk_idk
#AVDK=$HOME/reps/oss/bk_avdk
# Which build scripts/release.sh runs: build.sh (default) or build-remote.sh (the same build on
# REMOTE_BUILD_HOST, below).
#BUILD=build.sh
# Container runtime for the build scripts: podman if installed, else docker. Set to force one.
#CONTAINER_RUNTIME=podman

# ---- remote builder (scripts/build-remote.sh; docs/notes/remote-build.md) ----
# An x86-64 Linux host (or a WSL2 distro) with podman or docker, bk_idk and bk_avdk cloned at
# release/v2.0.1 and the bekencorp/armino-idk:1.5 image: the script rsyncs this working tree
# there, runs scripts/build.sh on it and copies the images back
# into FW_DIR. Only REMOTE_BUILD_HOST is required. Relative REMOTE_* paths are under the remote
# $HOME; keep them to plain path characters.
#REMOTE_BUILD_HOST=user@buildhost
#REMOTE_BUILD_PORT=22
#REMOTE_REPO_DIR=reps/home/iot/doorbell-bk7258-fw
#REMOTE_SDK=reps/oss/bk_idk
#REMOTE_AVDK=reps/oss/bk_avdk
#REMOTE_OUT=data/doorbell-bk7258/avdk-build
#REMOTE_FW_DIR=data/doorbell-bk7258/firmware
# Local shell command that brings the remote up when its ssh port does not answer (retried for
# 60 s afterwards). For a WSL2 distro: start its keep-alive task through the Windows OpenSSH, e.g.
#REMOTE_WAKE="ssh user@buildhost schtasks /run /tn my-wsl-keepalive"

# ---- Home Assistant (tools/ha_generic_camera.py) ----
# Base URL of your HA instance and the file holding a long-lived access token.
#HA_URL=http://homeassistant.local:8123
#HA_TOKEN_FILE=$HOME/.ha_token

# ---- OTA publishing (scripts/release.sh) ----
# HTTP base URL the DEVICE fetches images from (plain http, IPv4 literal). With HA serving
# /config/www/ as /local/ this is http://<ha-ip>:8123/local/doorbell
#OTA_URL_BASE=http://192.168.1.10:8123/local/doorbell
# Shell command that copies the image to wherever OTA_URL_BASE is served from. {rbl} is replaced
# by the full path of the image, {name} by its basename. Examples:
#OTA_PUBLISH="scp {rbl} user@ha:/config/www/doorbell/"
#OTA_PUBLISH="cp {rbl} /srv/http/doorbell/{name}"
